 "_note": "CDDA audio (tracks 2-17, the games music) is NOT part of this file manifest - those are Redbook audio tracks on the disc itself, ripped separately via CddaRipper, not files copied via this list. TRILOGY.ICO removed from rootFiles (Edward, 2026) - the original disc icon is low quality (8-bit); the executable now embeds a higher-quality icon directly at build time instead (see CMakeLists.txt WIN32 icon block), so GameLocator::Validate no longer checks for TRILOGY.ICO in the install directory, relying on CD/GFX/LEGAL.BND alone (already confirmed present on every release regardless of executable name, e.g. WTRILOGY.EXE on German releases). DiscLocator own disc-detection check is unaffected - the original disc still has the file, this only changes what gets copied during install. 121GFX.B16 removed from SECT11 (unused, per Edward - confirmed elsewhere on his end). SFX folder switched from copyAll to an explicit file list (Edward, 2026) - excludes unnecessary text files that told the original engine what SFX to load per level (irrelevant to our own engine), and a stray 3-byte file named \"E\" (bytes 0D 0A 1A). LANGUAGE folder keeps copyAll (the PNLGFX HUD files live there and are needed) but excludes *.BIN (Edward, 2026) - the seven .BIN files are the original's in-play text, now carried in LANGUAGE/<pack>/strings.txt as Gs* keys instead, so the binaries themselves are redundant. They are plain NUL-terminated string lists with no header, indexed by ordinal position; only ENGL, AMER and GERM were ever translated, the other four shipped as placeholders and fall back to English."
